-- allium: 3
-- accounts.allium — user accounts as identities: who a user is, how others see them, and how the account changes over its life.
--
-- Scope: the User identity (individual people, bots, remote/F3 placeholders,
-- ActivityPub mirrors, and the built-in system identities), its public profile,
-- its account status flags, its personal preferences, its email addresses, its
-- name (with renames, redirects and the reclaim cooldown), the social graph
-- (follow / block), account deletion and purge, and the profile README.
--
-- Includes:
--   - User (kinds, profile, status flags, preferences, avatar), Visibility
--   - EmailAddress (primary / secondary, activation, admin forced changes)
--   - UserRedirect (old names after a rename), username rules, reserved names,
--     USERNAME_PREFIX, USERNAME_COOLDOWN_PERIOD, MAX_USER_REDIRECTS
--   - Follow (user -> user or user -> organization)
--   - UserBlock (user or organization blocks a user) and the block enforcement
--     contract the other modules must honour
--   - UserSetting (per-user key/value preferences that change behaviour)
--   - Badge / UserBadge (profile badges)
--   - Account deletion (self / admin), purge, inactive-account cleanup cron
--   - Profile visibility (public / limited / private), keep-email-private,
--     keep-pronouns-private, keep-activity-private
--   - Profile README (`.profile` repository) and funding display rules
--   - Remote (F3) placeholder users being promoted to real accounts
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Registration forms, sign-in, passwords, 2FA, WebAuthn, OpenID URIs,
--     access tokens, OAuth2 apps, account activation mail / token checking,
--     password reset: owned by authentication (it emits the triggers this
--     module reacts to, see "Reacts to").
--   - SSH / GPG keys and their deletion on account removal: owned by keys.
--   - Organizations, teams, org membership, org renames: owned by organizations
--     (org renames create UserRedirect rows through RenameNamespace below).
--   - Quota: owned by quota.
--   - Activity feed, heatmap, RSS/Atom feeds, in-app notifications, mail
--     delivery: owned by notifications; this module only emits triggers and
--     exposes keep_activity_private / email_notifications.
--   - The explore/users search page and user search API: owned by discovery.
--   - Admin user management entry points (create user, edit status flags and
--     profile, set password / login source, set primary email, (de)activate
--     or delete addresses, rename, delete / purge, avatar, user list and
--     search, SystemNotice on cleanup failures) and the delete_inactive_accounts
--     cron task: owned by administration. This module reacts to its triggers
--     with the account-side consequences (redirects, purge cascade, cleanup).
--   - Service-message "confirm" timestamps (User.Confirms): owned by
--     administration (Announcement).
--   - FederatedUser / ActivityPub actor data, keys, inbox paths and remote
--     follows (FederatedUserFollower): owned by federation.
--   - "Wrong user type" doctor fix (CountWrongUserType/FixWrongUserType):
--     data-repair accident of the legacy schema, not behaviour.
--   - LastRepoVisibility (form convenience), Rands/Salt rotation (security
--     implementation detail), LowerName columns (case-insensitivity is stated
--     as an invariant instead).
--   - The X-Gitea-Warning header on admin email-domain conflicts: Gitea API
--     compatibility only; the behaviour (admin bypasses domain lists) is kept.
--   - Reserved user/organization placeholder rows (UserTypeUserReserved /
--     UserTypeOrganizationReserved): no code path creates them; parked as an
--     open question.
--
-- Emits:
--   UserAccountCreated(user)                       -- any new account
--   UserProfileUpdated(user)                       -- profile fields changed
--   UserRenamed(user, old_name, new_name)          -- repositories update owner names,
--                                                  -- packages update container image names,
--                                                  -- code moves AGit refs
--   UserVisibilityChanged(user, old_visibility, new_visibility)
--   UserAvatarChanged(user)
--   UserEmailAdded(user, address)                  -- notifications sends activation mail
--                                                  -- when confirmation is required
--   EmailActivationRequested(user, address)        -- authentication issues and mails a
--                                                  -- confirmation code (address is the string)
--   EmailAddressActivated(user, address)
--   PrimaryEmailChanged(user, old_address, new_address) -- notifications mails the old address
--   UserFollowed(follower, followee)
--   UserUnfollowed(follower, followee)
--   OrganizationFollowed(follower, organization)
--   UserBlocked(blocker, blocked)                  -- repositories: unwatch blocker's repos,
--                                                  -- drop collaboration, cancel transfers;
--                                                  -- actions: revoke trust
--   OrganizationBlockedUser(organization, blocked) -- same consequences for org-owned repos
--   UserUnblocked(blocker, blocked)
--   AccountStatusChanged(user)                     -- admin flags changed
--   UserPurged(user)                               -- purge began; repositories delete owned repos,
--                                                  -- organizations remove memberships and
--                                                  -- delete orgs where user is last owner,
--                                                  -- packages delete owned packages,
--                                                  -- federation deletes FederatedUser,
--                                                  -- authentication ends sessions
--   UserAccountDeleted(user, purge, delete_contributions)
--                                                  -- every module removes or ghosts the user's
--                                                  -- rows (see DeleteUserAccount guidance)
--
-- Reacts to:
--   authentication/UserSignedUp(user)              -- authentication created the account
--                                                  -- (every registration path); this module
--                                                  -- initialises the account-side records
--   authentication/RemoteUserClaimed(user, email)  -- OAuth2 login matched an F3 placeholder
--   authentication/EmailConfirmationLinkFollowed(user, email) -- mark the address activated
--   authentication/AccountActivated(user)          -- mark the primary address activated
--   authentication/UnconfirmedPrimaryEmailReplaced(user, new_address) -- swap the primary row
--   federation/RemoteActorDiscovered(name, full_name, email)
--   administration/UserRenamedByAdmin(admin, user, old_name, new_name)
--   administration/UserDeletedByAdmin(admin, user, purge)
--   administration/UserAvatarChangedByAdmin(admin, user)
--   administration/UserAvatarRemovedByAdmin(admin, user)
--   administration/InactiveAccountCleanupDue(older_than)

use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./administration.allium" as administration
use "./access.allium" as access

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Who can see a user (and, for organizations, the organization).
-- from: modules/structs/visible_type.go:12
enum Visibility { public | limited | private }

-- from: models/user/user.go:50
enum UserKind {
    individual      -- a person with a login
    | bot           -- automation account; behaves like an individual, labelled as a bot
    | remote        -- placeholder created by an F3 import for a person on another forge;
                    -- cannot log in until claimed through a matching OAuth2 login
    | activitypub   -- local mirror of a fediverse actor; never logs in
}

-- Built-in identities that are never stored and can never be registered.
-- from: models/user/user_system.go:20
enum SystemIdentity {
    ghost             -- stands in for a deleted account on everything it left behind
    | actions         -- "forgejo-actions": the doer of automated workflow changes
    | federation_actor -- "actor": the instance's own ActivityPub actor
}

-- from: models/user/user.go:75
enum EmailNotificationPreference {
    enabled           -- every notification mail except ones caused by the user
    | on_mention      -- only when mentioned
    | disabled
    | and_your_own    -- every notification mail including ones caused by the user
}

-- from: modules/setting/admin.go:31
enum UserFeature { deletion | manage_ssh_keys | manage_gpg_keys | manage_password }

-- How a user's avatar is resolved.
-- from: models/user/avatar.go:62
enum AvatarSource {
    uploaded          -- a custom image the user uploaded
    | generated       -- an identicon generated from the email (or name) seed
    | email_service   -- Gravatar / Libravatar, keyed on avatar_email
}

enum DiffViewStyle { unified | split }

-- from: routers/web/repo/middlewares.go:83
enum DiffWhitespaceBehaviour { show_all | ignore_all | ignore_change | ignore_eol }

-- Comment-type groups a user can hide from issue/PR timelines.
-- from: services/forms/user_form_hidden_comments.go:17
enum TimelineEventGroup {
    reference | label | milestone | assignee | title | branch | time_tracking
    | deadline | dependency | lock | review_request | pull_request_push
    | project | issue_ref
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An identity on the instance. Organizations are organizations/Organization,
-- but users and organizations share one namespace of names.
-- from: models/user/user.go:86
entity User {
    -- Identity
    name: String                         -- unique (case-insensitive) handle, renamable
    kind: UserKind
    created_at: Timestamp
    last_login_at: Timestamp?
    login_source: authentication/AuthSource?   -- null for local accounts

    -- Profile
    full_name: String                    -- max 100
    description: String                  -- "bio", Markdown, max 255
    website: String                      -- max 255, must use an allowed URL scheme
    location: String                     -- max 50
    pronouns: String                     -- max 50
    keep_pronouns_private: Boolean       -- hide pronouns from anonymous visitors
    keep_email_private: Boolean          -- show the no-reply address instead of the primary
    keep_activity_private: Boolean       -- hide activity feed and heatmap from others
    visibility: Visibility

    -- Avatar
    use_custom_avatar: Boolean
    custom_avatar: String?               -- stored image when uploaded or generated
    avatar_email: String                 -- address used for Gravatar/Libravatar lookups

    -- Contact
    primary_email: String
    email_notifications: EmailNotificationPreference

    -- Account status
    is_active: Boolean                   -- primary email confirmed / account activated
    is_admin: Boolean
    is_restricted: Boolean               -- only sees what it is explicitly given
    prohibit_login: Boolean              -- cannot sign in (git/SSH may still be allowed)

    -- Per-user capability overrides (admin managed)
    allow_git_hook: Boolean
    allow_import_local: Boolean
    allow_create_organization: Boolean
    max_repo_creation: Integer?          -- null means use the instance default

    -- Preferences
    language: String?                    -- null means use the browser / instance default
    theme: String
    diff_view_style: DiffViewStyle
    enable_repo_unit_hints: Boolean

    -- Relationships
    email_addresses: EmailAddress with user = this
    redirects: UserRedirect with user = this
    follows_given: Follow with follower = this
    follows_received: Follow with followee = this
    blocks_given: UserBlock with blocker = this
    blocks_received: UserBlock with blocked = this
    settings: UserSetting with user = this
    badges: UserBadge with user = this

    -- Projections
    followers: follows_received -> follower
    following_users: follows_given where followee != null -> followee
    activated_emails: email_addresses where is_activated = true
    primary_address: email_addresses where is_primary = true

    -- Derived
    num_followers: follows_received.count
    num_following: follows_given.count
    is_local: login_source = null
    is_system: false                     -- stored users are never system identities
    no_reply_email: name + "@" + config.no_reply_address
    public_email: if keep_email_private: no_reply_email else: primary_email
    display_name: if full_name != "": full_name else: name
    can_sign_in: is_active and not prohibit_login
    can_receive_mail: is_active and not prohibit_login and kind = individual
    avatar_source:
        if use_custom_avatar: uploaded
        else: if config.disable_gravatar: generated
        else: email_service
    effective_repo_limit:
        if max_repo_creation != null: max_repo_creation
        else: config.max_repo_creation_default
    can_create_organization: is_admin or (allow_create_organization and not config.org_creation_disabled)
    can_edit_git_hooks: not config.disable_git_hooks and (is_admin or allow_git_hook)
    can_import_local: config.import_local_paths and (is_admin or allow_import_local)
    pronouns_for(signed_in): if keep_pronouns_private and not signed_in: "" else: pronouns
    activity_readable_by(viewer): not keep_activity_private or viewer.is_admin or viewer = this
    has_feature_disabled(f):
        f in config.user_disabled_features
        or (not is_local and f in config.external_user_disabled_features)

    -- Who may see this profile (and therefore resolve its name, its followers
    -- lists and its redirects). Admins and the user always can. Public: everyone.
    -- Limited: any signed-in, non-restricted user. Private: signed-in,
    -- non-restricted users this user follows, or who share an organization.
    -- from: models/user/user.go:1402
    visible_to(viewer):
        viewer.is_admin
        or viewer = this
        or visibility = public
        or (visibility = limited and not viewer.is_restricted)
        or (visibility = private and not viewer.is_restricted
            and (exists Follow{follower: this, followee: viewer} or shares_organization(this, viewer)))
}

-- One address of a user. Every address is unique across the instance
-- (case-insensitive); exactly one per user is primary.
-- from: models/user/email_address.go:79
entity EmailAddress {
    user: User
    address: String                      -- max 254
    is_activated: Boolean
    is_primary: Boolean

    can_be_primary: is_activated
}

-- An old name of a user (or organization) that still resolves to it.
-- from: models/user/redirect.go:52
entity UserRedirect {
    old_name: String
    user: User?                          -- set when the namespace owner is a user
    organization: organizations/Organization?   -- set when it is an organization
    created_at: Timestamp

    cooldown_ends_at: created_at + config.username_cooldown_period
    in_cooldown: config.username_cooldown_period > 0.days and cooldown_ends_at > now
}

-- A user following another user or an organization.
-- from: models/user/follow.go:15
entity Follow {
    follower: User
    followee: User?
    followee_organization: organizations/Organization?
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- A block. The blocker is a user or an organization; the blocked party is
-- always a user.
-- from: models/user/block.go:18
entity UserBlock {
    blocker: User?
    blocker_organization: organizations/Organization?
    blocked: User
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- Per-user preference with behaviour elsewhere in the system.
-- from: models/user/setting.go:20
entity UserSetting {
    user: User
    key: hidden_timeline_events | diff_whitespace_behaviour | show_outdated_review_comments
    value: String
}

-- A badge an instance can award; shown on profiles.
-- from: models/user/badge.go:12
entity Badge {
    description: String
    image_url: String
}

-- from: models/user/badge.go:18
entity UserBadge {
    badge: Badge
    user: User
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [service]
    default_keep_email_private: Boolean = false              -- DEFAULT_KEEP_EMAIL_PRIVATE
    default_allow_create_organization: Boolean = true        -- DEFAULT_ALLOW_CREATE_ORGANIZATION
    default_user_is_restricted: Boolean = false              -- DEFAULT_USER_IS_RESTRICTED
    default_user_visibility: Visibility = public             -- DEFAULT_USER_VISIBILITY (first allowed mode)
    allowed_user_visibility_modes: Set<Visibility> = { public, limited, private }  -- ALLOWED_USER_VISIBILITY_MODES
    allow_dots_in_usernames: Boolean = true                  -- ALLOW_DOTS_IN_USERNAMES
    username_prefix: String = ""                             -- USERNAME_PREFIX, applied on self-registration
    username_cooldown_period: Duration = 0.days              -- USERNAME_COOLDOWN_PERIOD (days); 0 disables
    max_user_redirects: Integer = 0                          -- MAX_USER_REDIRECTS; defaults to 5 when a cooldown is set; 0 = unlimited
    no_reply_address: String = "noreply.localhost"           -- NO_REPLY_ADDRESS, default "noreply." + DOMAIN
    user_location_map_url: String = "https://www.openstreetmap.org/search?query="  -- USER_LOCATION_MAP_URL
    valid_site_url_schemes: Set<String> = { "http", "https" }  -- VALID_SITE_URL_SCHEMES (website field)
    user_delete_with_comments_max_time: Duration = 0.days    -- USER_DELETE_WITH_COMMENTS_MAX_TIME; 0 disables
    require_email_confirmation: Boolean = false              -- REGISTER_EMAIL_CONFIRM (shared with authentication)
    require_manual_confirmation: Boolean = false             -- REGISTER_MANUAL_CONFIRM (shared with authentication)
    email_domain_allowlist: Set<String> = {}                 -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_ALLOWLIST (globs)
    email_domain_blocklist: Set<String> = {}                 -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCKLIST (globs)
    email_domain_block_disposable: Boolean = false           -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCK_DISPOSABLE
    activation_link_lifetime: Duration = 180.minutes         -- ACTIVE_CODE_LIVE_MINUTES
    activation_resend_cooldown: Duration = 3.minutes         -- hard-coded mail resend limit

    -- [admin]
    -- DISABLE_REGULAR_ORG_CREATION is owned by organizations; read here, not redeclared.
    org_creation_disabled: Boolean = organizations/config.disable_regular_org_creation
    default_email_notifications: EmailNotificationPreference = enabled  -- DEFAULT_EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS
    user_disabled_features: Set<UserFeature> = {}            -- USER_DISABLED_FEATURES
    external_user_disabled_features: Set<UserFeature> = {}   -- EXTERNAL_USER_DISABLE_FEATURES

    -- [picture]
    avatar_max_width: Integer = 4096                         -- AVATAR_MAX_WIDTH (pixels)
    avatar_max_height: Integer = 4096                        -- AVATAR_MAX_HEIGHT (pixels)
    avatar_max_file_size: Integer = 1048576                  -- AVATAR_MAX_FILE_SIZE (bytes)
    avatar_max_origin_size: Integer = 262144                 -- AVATAR_MAX_ORIGIN_SIZE: smaller uploads are stored unprocessed
    avatar_rendered_size_factor: Integer = 2                 -- AVATAR_RENDERED_SIZE_FACTOR
    gravatar_source: String = "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/"  -- GRAVATAR_SOURCE ("gravatar" | "libravatar" | URL)
    disable_gravatar: Boolean = false                        -- DISABLE_GRAVATAR (true in OFFLINE_MODE); runtime-editable
    enable_federated_avatar: Boolean = false                 -- ENABLE_FEDERATED_AVATAR (Libravatar DNS lookup); runtime-editable

    -- [ui]
    show_user_email: Boolean = true                          -- SHOW_USER_EMAIL
    default_show_full_name: Boolean = false                  -- DEFAULT_SHOW_FULL_NAME
    default_theme: String = "forgejo-auto"                   -- DEFAULT_THEME
    themes: Set<String> = { "forgejo-auto", "forgejo-light", "forgejo-dark", "gitea-auto", "gitea-light", "gitea-dark", "forgejo-auto-deuteranopia-protanopia", "forgejo-light-deuteranopia-protanopia", "forgejo-dark-deuteranopia-protanopia", "forgejo-auto-tritanopia", "forgejo-light-tritanopia", "forgejo-dark-tritanopia" }  -- THEMES
    languages: Set<String> = { "en-US" }                     -- [i18n] LANGS (abbreviated)

    -- Capability defaults that live in other sections but are evaluated on User
    max_repo_creation_default: Integer = -1                  -- [repository] MAX_CREATION_LIMIT; -1 = unlimited
    disable_git_hooks: Boolean = true                        -- [security] DISABLE_GIT_HOOKS
    import_local_paths: Boolean = false                      -- [security] IMPORT_LOCAL_PATHS
    packages_enabled: Boolean = true                         -- [packages] ENABLED
    federation_enabled: Boolean = false                      -- [federation] ENABLED

    -- [cron.delete_inactive_accounts] ENABLED / SCHEDULE / OLDER_THAN belong to
    -- administration's CronTask, which passes OLDER_THAN (default
    -- ACTIVE_CODE_LIVE_MINUTES) in InactiveAccountCleanupDue.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Names
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A name is usable when it matches the username pattern and is not reserved.
-- Pattern: starts with a letter or digit; then letters, digits, '-', '_' and
-- (when allowed) '.'; no two consecutive '-', '_', '.' and no trailing one;
-- max 40 characters. Reserved: ".", "..", "-", ".well-known", "api",
-- "metrics", "v2", "assets", "attachments", "avatar", "avatars",
-- "repo-avatars", "captcha", "login", "org", "repo", "user", "admin",
-- "explore", "issues", "pulls", "milestones", "notifications",
-- "report_abuse", "favicon.ico", "manifest.json", "robots.txt",
-- "sitemap.xml", "ssh_info", "swagger.v1.json", "ghost", "gitea-actions",
-- "forgejo-actions", "actor"; reserved patterns "*.keys", "*.gpg", "*.rss",
-- "*.atom", "*.png". All comparisons are case-insensitive. Lookups by
-- name or address (UserRedirect{old_name}, EmailAddress{address}) are
-- case-insensitive too.
-- ActivityPub mirrors instead use the handle form "@user@host[:port]".
-- from: models/user/user.go:621

-- Self-registration, on every path (sign-up form, external-login
-- auto-registration, reverse-proxy and directory provisioning). authentication
-- owns the registration checks and creates the accounts/User (the same act
-- binds the session and the UserLogin to it) and emits UserSignedUp; this
-- module then initialises the account-side records and defaults.
-- Name rules applied by authentication's checks: USERNAME_PREFIX is prepended
-- when set and missing; the name must be usable, free, and not a redirect
-- still in its cooldown; the address must be valid, allowed and unused.
-- from: models/user/user.go:681
rule InitialiseSelfRegisteredAccount {
    when: authentication/UserSignedUp(user)
    ensures: user.created_at = now
    ensures: user.full_name = ""
    ensures: user.keep_email_private = config.default_keep_email_private
    ensures: user.keep_pronouns_private = false
    ensures: user.keep_activity_private = false
    ensures: user.visibility = config.default_user_visibility
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = false
    ensures: user.avatar_email = user.primary_email
    ensures: user.email_notifications = config.default_email_notifications
    ensures: user.allow_git_hook = false
    ensures: user.allow_import_local = false
    ensures: user.allow_create_organization = config.default_allow_create_organization and not config.org_creation_disabled
    ensures: user.theme = config.default_theme
    ensures: user.diff_view_style = unified
    ensures: user.enable_repo_unit_hints = true
    ensures:
        if not exists EmailAddress{address: user.primary_email}:
            EmailAddress.created(user: user, address: user.primary_email, is_activated: user.is_active, is_primary: true)
    ensures:
        for r in UserRedirects where same_name(old_name, user.name):
            not exists r
    ensures: UserAccountCreated(user: user)
}

-- A fediverse actor seen for the first time gets a local mirror account.
-- from: services/federation/federation_service.go:232
rule CreateActivityPubMirror {
    when: RemoteActorDiscovered(handle, full_name, email)
    requires: config.federation_enabled
    requires: is_valid_activitypub_handle(handle)
    requires: not name_taken(handle)
    ensures:
        let user = User.created(
            name: handle,
            kind: activitypub,
            created_at: now,
            full_name: full_name,
            description: "", website: "", location: "", pronouns: "",
            keep_pronouns_private: false,
            keep_email_private: true,
            keep_activity_private: false,
            visibility: config.default_user_visibility,
            use_custom_avatar: false,
            avatar_email: email,
            primary_email: email,
            email_notifications: disabled,
            is_active: false,
            is_admin: false,
            is_restricted: false,
            prohibit_login: true,
            allow_git_hook: false,
            allow_import_local: false,
            allow_create_organization: false,
            theme: config.default_theme,
            diff_view_style: unified,
            enable_repo_unit_hints: true
        )
        EmailAddress.created(user: user, address: email, is_activated: false, is_primary: true)
        UserAccountCreated(user: user)
}

-- An F3 placeholder is promoted to a real account when its person signs in
-- through the OAuth2 source that matches the placeholder's remote source.
-- from: services/remote/promote.go:52
rule PromoteRemoteUser {
    when: RemoteUserClaimed(user, email)
    requires: user.kind = remote
    requires: user.primary_email = ""
    requires: not exists EmailAddress{address: email}
    ensures: user.kind = individual
    ensures: user.primary_email = email
    ensures: user.prohibit_login = false
    ensures: EmailAddress.created(user: user, address: email, is_activated: true, is_primary: true)
    ensures: AccountStatusChanged(user: user)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Renaming
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user renames themselves. Only local accounts, or accounts whose OAuth2
-- source allows username changes, may do so. A case-only change keeps
-- everything else as is. Otherwise the old name becomes a redirect, only
-- the newest MAX_USER_REDIRECTS redirects are kept, and a name whose
-- redirect is still cooling down can only be reclaimed by its former owner
-- (or, for an organization's old name, by that organization's owners).
-- Web: POST /user/settings (name field). There is no self-rename API.
-- from: services/user/user.go:69
rule UserRenamesSelf {
    when: UserRenamesSelf(user, new_name)
    requires: new_name != user.name
    requires: user.login_source = null or user.login_source.allows_username_change
    requires: is_usable_username(new_name)
    requires: same_name(new_name, user.name) or not name_taken(new_name)
    let claimed = UserRedirect{old_name: new_name}
    requires: not exists claimed
        or not claimed.in_cooldown
        or claimed.user = user
        or (claimed.organization != null and is_org_owner(claimed.organization, user))
    ensures: RenameNamespace(user: user, old_name: user.name, new_name: new_name)
}

-- A site admin renamed a user (administration owns the entry point; it skips
-- the login-source and cooldown checks). The old name is kept as a redirect
-- exactly as for a self rename.
-- API: POST /admin/users/{username}/rename. Web: /-/admin/users/{id}/edit.
-- from: services/user/user.go:48
rule AdminRenameKeepsRedirect {
    when: administration/UserRenamedByAdmin(admin, user, old_name, new_name)
    ensures: RenameNamespace(user: user, old_name: old_name, new_name: new_name)
}

-- The common half of a rename.
-- from: services/user/user.go:107
rule RenameNamespace {
    when: RenameNamespace(user, old_name, new_name)
    let case_only = same_name(old_name, new_name)
    ensures: user.name = new_name
    ensures:
        if not case_only:
            for r in UserRedirects where same_name(old_name, old_name) or same_name(old_name, new_name):
                not exists r
            UserRedirect.created(old_name: old_name, user: user, created_at: now)
    ensures: UserRenamed(user: user, old_name: old_name, new_name: new_name)
    @guidance
        -- When MAX_USER_REDIRECTS > 0, delete this user's oldest redirects
        -- beyond that count (see LimitUserRedirects).
        -- Consumers of UserRenamed: repositories (owner name on every owned
        -- repository and on-disk location), packages (container image names),
        -- code (AGit refs that embed the user name).
}

-- Keep only the newest MAX_USER_REDIRECTS redirects per user.
-- from: models/user/redirect.go:97
rule LimitUserRedirects {
    when: redirect: UserRedirect.created
    requires: config.max_user_redirects > 0
    requires: redirect.user != null
    requires: redirect.user.redirects.count > config.max_user_redirects
    ensures:
        for r in oldest_redirects(redirect.user, redirect.user.redirects.count - config.max_user_redirects):
            not exists r
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Profile, preferences, avatar
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Web: POST /user/settings. API: PATCH /user/settings (subset: full_name,
-- description, pronouns, website, location, hide_email, hide_pronouns,
-- hide_activity).
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:72
rule UserUpdatesProfile {
    when: UserUpdatesProfile(user, full_name, description, website, location, pronouns, keep_email_private, keep_pronouns_private, keep_activity_private)
    requires: length(full_name) <= 100
    requires: length(description) <= 255
    requires: length(website) <= 255
    requires: website = "" or url_scheme(website) in config.valid_site_url_schemes
    requires: length(location) <= 50
    requires: length(pronouns) <= 50
    ensures: user.full_name = full_name
    ensures: user.description = description
    ensures: user.website = website
    ensures: user.location = location
    ensures: user.pronouns = pronouns
    ensures: user.keep_email_private = keep_email_private
    ensures: user.keep_pronouns_private = keep_pronouns_private
    ensures: user.keep_activity_private = keep_activity_private
    ensures: UserProfileUpdated(user: user)
}

-- Visibility is changed from the same profile form; only modes the
-- instance allows are accepted.
-- from: services/user/update.go:131
rule UserChangesVisibility {
    when: UserChangesVisibility(user, visibility)
    requires: visibility in config.allowed_user_visibility_modes
    requires: visibility != user.visibility
    ensures: user.visibility = visibility
    ensures: UserVisibilityChanged(user: user, old_visibility: user.visibility, new_visibility: visibility)
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/appearance/theme. API: PATCH /user/settings (theme).
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:351
rule UserChangesTheme {
    when: UserChangesTheme(user, theme)
    requires: theme in config.themes
    ensures: user.theme = theme
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/appearance/language. API: PATCH /user/settings (language).
-- An empty language means "follow the browser".
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:378
rule UserChangesLanguage {
    when: UserChangesLanguage(user, language)
    requires: language = null or language in config.languages
    ensures: user.language = language
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/appearance/hints. API: PATCH /user/settings.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:408
rule UserTogglesRepoUnitHints {
    when: UserTogglesRepoUnitHints(user, enabled)
    ensures: user.enable_repo_unit_hints = enabled
}

-- Remembered whenever the user switches the diff view; also API PATCH /user/settings.
-- from: routers/web/repo/middlewares.go:39
rule UserChangesDiffViewStyle {
    when: UserChangesDiffViewStyle(user, style)
    ensures: user.diff_view_style = style
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/appearance/hidden_comments.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:426
rule UserHidesTimelineEvents {
    when: UserHidesTimelineEvents(user, groups)
    let existing = UserSetting{user: user, key: hidden_timeline_events}
    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            existing.value = encode_groups(groups)
        else:
            UserSetting.created(user: user, key: hidden_timeline_events, value: encode_groups(groups))
}

-- Remembered whenever the user picks a whitespace mode on a diff.
-- from: routers/web/repo/middlewares.go:83
rule UserChangesDiffWhitespace {
    when: UserChangesDiffWhitespace(user, behaviour)
    let existing = UserSetting{user: user, key: diff_whitespace_behaviour}
    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            existing.value = encode_whitespace(behaviour)
        else:
            UserSetting.created(user: user, key: diff_whitespace_behaviour, value: encode_whitespace(behaviour))
}

-- Remembered whenever the user toggles outdated review comments on a PR.
-- from: routers/web/repo/middlewares.go:109
rule UserTogglesOutdatedComments {
    when: UserTogglesOutdatedComments(user, show)
    let existing = UserSetting{user: user, key: show_outdated_review_comments}
    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            existing.value = encode_boolean(show)
        else:
            UserSetting.created(user: user, key: show_outdated_review_comments, value: encode_boolean(show))
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/email with _method=NOTIFICATION.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/account.go:186
rule UserChangesEmailNotifications {
    when: UserChangesEmailNotifications(user, preference)
    ensures: user.email_notifications = preference
}

-- Upload a custom avatar. Only PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP; never SVG; at most
-- AVATAR_MAX_FILE_SIZE bytes and AVATAR_MAX_WIDTH x AVATAR_MAX_HEIGHT pixels.
-- Images at or above AVATAR_MAX_ORIGIN_SIZE are centre-cropped to a square
-- and scaled; the smaller of original and processed is kept.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/avatar (source=local). API: POST /user/avatar (base64).
-- from: services/user/avatar.go:20
rule UserUploadsAvatar {
    when: UserUploadsAvatar(user, image)
    requires: image_format(image) in { "png", "jpeg", "gif", "webp" }
    requires: byte_size(image) <= config.avatar_max_file_size
    requires: image_width(image) <= config.avatar_max_width
    requires: image_height(image) <= config.avatar_max_height
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = true
    ensures: user.custom_avatar = store_avatar(user, image)
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

-- Choose the email-keyed avatar service (Gravatar / Libravatar) and the
-- address it is keyed on. The address must pass the email-domain lists.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/avatar (source=bymail).
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:126
rule UserChoosesEmailAvatar {
    when: UserChoosesEmailAvatar(user, avatar_email)
    requires: is_valid_email(avatar_email) and email_domain_allowed(avatar_email)
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = false
    ensures: user.avatar_email = avatar_email
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

-- Switching to "custom" without an upload generates an identicon.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/profile.go:146
rule UserSwitchesToGeneratedAvatar {
    when: UserSwitchesToGeneratedAvatar(user)
    requires: user.custom_avatar = null
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = true
    ensures: user.custom_avatar = generate_identicon(user)
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

-- Web: POST /user/settings/avatar/delete. API: DELETE /user/avatar.
-- from: services/user/avatar.go:53
rule UserDeletesAvatar {
    when: UserDeletesAvatar(user)
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = false
    ensures: user.custom_avatar = null
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

-- An admin uploaded or removed a user's avatar (administration owns the
-- entry points; the same image limits apply).
-- from: routers/web/admin/users.go:542
rule AdminAvatarChangeApplies {
    when: administration/UserAvatarChangedByAdmin(admin, user)
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = true
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

-- from: routers/web/admin/users.go:559
rule AdminAvatarRemovalApplies {
    when: administration/UserAvatarRemovedByAdmin(admin, user)
    ensures: user.use_custom_avatar = false
    ensures: user.custom_avatar = null
    ensures: UserAvatarChanged(user: user)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Email addresses
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Add one or more secondary addresses. With confirmation required they start
-- unactivated and an activation mail is sent; adding is blocked while an
-- activation mail sent in the last few minutes is pending.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/email. API: POST /user/emails (list).
-- from: services/user/email.go:120
rule UserAddsEmail {
    when: UserAddsEmail(user, address)
    requires: length(address) <= 254
    requires: is_valid_email(address) and email_domain_allowed(address)
    requires: not exists EmailAddress{address: address}
    ensures:
        let added = EmailAddress.created(user: user, address: address, is_activated: not config.require_email_confirmation, is_primary: false)
        UserEmailAdded(user: user, address: address)
}

-- Resend an activation mail for an unactivated address (rate limited).
-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/email with _method=SENDACTIVATION.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/account.go:131
rule UserResendsEmailActivation {
    when: UserResendsEmailActivation(user, address)
    requires: address.user = user
    requires: not address.is_activated
    requires: not activation_mail_recently_sent(user)
    ensures: EmailActivationRequested(user: user, address: address.address)
}

-- The user followed a valid confirmation link. authentication owns the link,
-- the code and the page (UserConfirmsEmailAddress, UserActivatesAccount); this
-- module marks the address record. Activating the primary address also
-- activates the account. An address already active on another account cannot
-- be activated.
-- from: models/user/email_address.go:367
rule ConfirmedAddressIsActivated {
    when: authentication/EmailConfirmationLinkFollowed(user, email)
    let address = EmailAddress{address: email}
    requires: address.user = user
    requires: not address.is_activated
    requires: not activated_elsewhere(address)
    ensures: address.is_activated = true
    ensures:
        if address.is_primary:
            user.is_active = true
    ensures: EmailAddressActivated(user: user, address: address)
}

-- An activated account has an activated primary address.
-- from: models/user/user.go:1105
rule ActivatedAccountActivatesPrimaryAddress {
    when: authentication/AccountActivated(user)
    ensures:
        for e in user.email_addresses where is_primary:
            e.is_activated = true
}

-- Make an activated secondary address the primary; the old primary stays as
-- a secondary address and is told about the change.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/email with _method=PRIMARY.
-- from: services/user/email.go:217
rule UserMakesEmailPrimary {
    when: UserMakesEmailPrimary(user, address)
    requires: address.user = user
    requires: address.is_activated
    requires: not address.is_primary
    let old_primary = user.primary_email
    ensures:
        for e in user.email_addresses where is_primary:
            e.is_primary = false
    ensures: address.is_primary = true
    ensures: user.primary_email = address.address
    ensures: PrimaryEmailChanged(user: user, old_address: old_primary, new_address: address.address)
}

-- An unactivated account replaced its (unconfirmed) primary address, e.g.
-- after a typo during registration. authentication owns the entry point, its
-- checks and the fresh activation code (InactiveUserReplacesUnconfirmedEmail);
-- this module swaps the address record.
-- from: services/user/email.go:168
rule InactivePrimaryEmailReplaced {
    when: authentication/UnconfirmedPrimaryEmailReplaced(user, new_address)
    ensures:
        for e in user.email_addresses where is_primary:
            not exists e
        EmailAddress.created(user: user, address: new_address, is_activated: false, is_primary: true)
        user.primary_email = new_address
}

-- Remove secondary addresses; the primary can never be removed.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/email/delete. API: DELETE /user/emails.
-- from: services/user/email.go:194
rule UserDeletesEmail {
    when: UserDeletesEmail(user, address)
    requires: address.user = user
    requires: not address.is_primary
    ensures: not exists address
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Following
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Web: POST /{username} action=follow. API: PUT /user/following/{username}.
-- Following an organization uses the same endpoint on the org's name.
-- from: models/user/follow.go:31
rule UserFollowsUser {
    when: UserFollowsUser(follower, followee)
    requires: follower != followee
    requires: not exists Follow{follower: follower, followee: followee}
    requires: not exists UserBlock{blocker: follower, blocked: followee}
    requires: not exists UserBlock{blocker: followee, blocked: follower}
    requires: followee.visible_to(follower)
    ensures: Follow.created(follower: follower, followee: followee, created_at: now)
    ensures: UserFollowed(follower: follower, followee: followee)
}

-- from: routers/web/user/profile.go:426
rule UserFollowsOrganization {
    when: UserFollowsOrganization(follower, organization)
    requires: not exists Follow{follower: follower, followee_organization: organization}
    requires: not organization_has_blocked(organization, follower)
    ensures: Follow.created(follower: follower, followee_organization: organization, created_at: now)
    ensures: OrganizationFollowed(follower: follower, organization: organization)
}

-- Web: POST /{username} action=unfollow. API: DELETE /user/following/{username}.
-- from: models/user/follow.go:60
rule UserUnfollowsUser {
    when: UserUnfollowsUser(follower, followee)
    let follow = Follow{follower: follower, followee: followee}
    requires: exists follow
    ensures: not exists follow
    ensures: UserUnfollowed(follower: follower, followee: followee)
}

-- from: models/user/follow.go:60
rule UserUnfollowsOrganization {
    when: UserUnfollowsOrganization(follower, organization)
    let follow = Follow{follower: follower, followee_organization: organization}
    requires: exists follow
    ensures: not exists follow
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Blocking
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user blocks another user. Both follow relationships are dropped at once;
-- the remaining consequences (unwatch the blocker's repositories, drop the
-- blocked user's collaboration on them, cancel pending transfers between the
-- two, revoke Actions trust on the blocker's repositories) happen in the
-- modules that own those things, reacting to UserBlocked.
-- Organizations cannot be blocked through this rule.
-- Web: POST /{username} action=block. API: PUT /user/block/{username}.
-- from: services/user/block.go:21
rule UserBlocksUser {
    when: UserBlocksUser(blocker, blocked)
    requires: blocker != blocked
    requires: not exists UserBlock{blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked}
    ensures: UserBlock.created(blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked, created_at: now)
    ensures: not exists Follow{follower: blocker, followee: blocked}
    ensures: not exists Follow{follower: blocked, followee: blocker}
    ensures: UserBlocked(blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked)
}

-- Web: POST /{username} action=unblock, POST /user/settings/blocked_users/unblock.
-- API: PUT /user/unblock/{username}.
-- from: models/user/block.go:47
rule UserUnblocksUser {
    when: UserUnblocksUser(blocker, blocked)
    let block = UserBlock{blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked}
    requires: exists block
    ensures: not exists block
    ensures: UserUnblocked(blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked)
}

-- An organization owner blocks a user on behalf of the organization.
-- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings/blocked_users/block. API: PUT /orgs/{org}/block/{username}.
-- from: routers/web/org/setting/blocked_users.go:62
rule OrganizationBlocksUser {
    when: OrganizationBlocksUser(owner, organization, blocked)
    requires: is_org_owner(organization, owner) or owner.is_admin
    requires: not organization_has_blocked(organization, blocked)
    ensures: UserBlock.created(blocker_organization: organization, blocked: blocked, created_at: now)
    ensures: not exists Follow{follower: blocked, followee_organization: organization}
    ensures: OrganizationBlockedUser(organization: organization, blocked: blocked)
}

-- Web: POST /org/{org}/settings/blocked_users/unblock. API: PUT /orgs/{org}/unblock/{username}.
-- from: routers/web/org/setting/blocked_users.go:80
rule OrganizationUnblocksUser {
    when: OrganizationUnblocksUser(owner, organization, blocked)
    let block = UserBlock{blocker_organization: organization, blocked: blocked}
    requires: is_org_owner(organization, owner) or owner.is_admin
    requires: exists block
    ensures: not exists block
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deletion
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user deletes their own account after re-entering their password
-- (checked by authentication). Admins cannot delete themselves; the
-- "deletion" feature can be disabled per instance (or for external users);
-- the account must own no repositories or packages and belong to no
-- organization.
-- Web: POST /user/settings/account/delete. No API.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/account.go:240
rule UserDeletesOwnAccount {
    when: UserDeletesOwnAccount(user)
    requires: not deletion_disabled_for(user)   -- = user.has_feature_disabled(deletion)
    requires: not user.is_admin
    requires: not owns_repositories(user)
    requires: not belongs_to_organizations(user)
    requires: not owns_packages(user)
    ensures: DeleteUserAccount(user: user, purge: false)
}

-- A site admin deleted an account (administration owns the entry point and
-- its preconditions: not self, not the last admin, purge or owns nothing).
-- With purge the account is disabled at once, then everything it owns is
-- removed by the owning modules, then the account itself.
-- API: DELETE /admin/users/{username}?purge=. Web: POST /-/admin/users/{id}/delete.
-- from: services/user/user.go:183
rule AdminDeletionCascades {
    when: administration/UserDeletedByAdmin(admin, user, purge)
    ensures:
        if purge:
            user.is_active = false
            user.is_restricted = true
            user.is_admin = false
            user.prohibit_login = true
            user.max_repo_creation = 0
            UserPurged(user: user)
        DeleteUserAccount(user: user, purge: purge)
}

-- The removal itself. Things this module owns go here; everything else
-- reacts to UserAccountDeleted.
-- from: services/user/delete.go:36
rule DeleteUserAccount {
    when: DeleteUserAccount(user, purge)
    let young = config.user_delete_with_comments_max_time > 0.days
                and user.created_at + config.user_delete_with_comments_max_time > now
    ensures:
        for e in user.email_addresses: not exists e
        for f in user.follows_given: not exists f
        for f in user.follows_received: not exists f
        for b in user.blocks_given: not exists b
        for b in user.blocks_received: not exists b
        for s in user.settings: not exists s
        for ub in user.badges: not exists ub
        for r in user.redirects: not exists r
        UserAccountDeleted(user: user, purge: purge, delete_contributions: purge or young)
        not exists user
    @guidance
        -- Consumers of UserAccountDeleted, all keyed on the user:
        --   repositories: stars, watches (and their counters), collaborations,
        --     derived access rows.
        --   issues: reactions, stopwatches, assignments, issue-user state;
        --     tracked time is kept but detached; if delete_contributions,
        --     the user's plain comments and reactions are deleted, and if
        --     purge, every issue/PR they opened is deleted; otherwise
        --     their content stays and shows as the ghost user.
        --   pulls: auto-merge requests, review state.
        --   code: the user disappears from branch-protection allow-lists.
        --   keys: SSH keys (authorized_keys rewritten), GPG keys and imports.
        --   authentication: access tokens and their repo scopes, OAuth2
        --     grants/apps, external logins, OpenID URIs, authorization
        --     tokens, authorized integrations.
        --   organizations: team memberships, team invites sent or received;
        --     the "added by" provenance on team memberships is cleared.
        --   actions: user-owned runners and runner tokens, action-user trust.
        --   notifications: the user's activity rows.
        --   moderation: a shadow copy is kept if the user was reported.
        -- On-disk repository root and stored avatar are removed last;
        -- failures there become a system notice (administration).
}

-- Unactivated individual accounts older than OLDER_THAN are removed when
-- administration's delete_inactive_accounts cron task runs (disabled by
-- default, @annually when enabled, runnable on demand). Accounts that own
-- something, belong to an organization, or are the last admin are skipped.
-- from: services/user/user.go:363
rule DeleteInactiveAccounts {
    when: administration/InactiveAccountCleanupDue(older_than)
    for user in Users where is_active = false and kind = individual:
        requires: user.created_at + older_than <= now
        requires: not owns_repositories(user)
        requires: not belongs_to_organizations(user)
        requires: not owns_packages(user)
        requires: not (user.is_admin and admin_count() <= 1)
        ensures: DeleteUserAccount(user: user, purge: false)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Names are unique case-insensitively across users and organizations.
-- from: models/user/user.go:86 (UNIQUE lower_name)
invariant UniqueUserNames {
    for a in Users:
        for b in Users:
            a = b or not same_name(a.name, b.name)
}

-- Addresses are unique case-insensitively across the instance.
-- from: models/user/email_address.go:82
invariant UniqueEmailAddresses {
    for a in EmailAddresses:
        for b in EmailAddresses:
            a = b or not same_address(a.address, b.address)
}

-- Every account that has addresses has exactly one primary, and it matches
-- User.primary_email.
invariant SinglePrimaryEmail {
    for u in Users:
        u.email_addresses.count = 0
        or (u.primary_address.count = 1
            and u.primary_address.all(e => e.address = u.primary_email))
}

-- An unactivated primary address means an unactivated account.
invariant ActiveAccountHasActivatedPrimary {
    for e in EmailAddresses:
        not e.is_primary or e.is_activated or not e.user.is_active or not config.require_email_confirmation
}

-- There is always at least one site admin once the instance is installed.
invariant AtLeastOneAdmin {
    Users.any(u => u.is_admin)
}

-- No one follows or blocks themselves.
invariant NoSelfFollow {
    for f in Follows:
        f.followee != f.follower
}

invariant NoSelfBlock {
    for b in UserBlocks:
        b.blocker != b.blocked
}

-- A block and a follow never coexist between the same two users.
invariant BlockSeversFollow {
    for b in UserBlocks:
        b.blocker = null
        or not Follows.any(f =>
            (f.follower = b.blocker and f.followee = b.blocked)
            or (f.follower = b.blocked and f.followee = b.blocker))
}

-- Exactly one followee kind and one blocker kind.
invariant FollowHasOneTarget {
    for f in Follows:
        (f.followee != null) != (f.followee_organization != null)
}

invariant BlockHasOneBlocker {
    for b in UserBlocks:
        (b.blocker != null) != (b.blocker_organization != null)
}

invariant RedirectHasOneTarget {
    for r in UserRedirects:
        (r.user != null) != (r.organization != null)
}

-- An old name never shadows a live name.
invariant RedirectNeverShadowsLiveName {
    for r in UserRedirects:
        not Users.any(u => same_name(u.name, r.old_name))
}

-- User visibility is always one of the instance's allowed modes at the
-- time it was set (organizations are exempt; see organizations).
invariant VisibilityAllowed {
    for u in Users:
        u.visibility in config.allowed_user_visibility_modes
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Signed-in users are access/SignedInUser; organization owners are
-- organizations/OrgOwner. An unactivated account's activation page is
-- authentication/AccountActivation.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The account holder's own settings: profile, appearance, avatar.
surface OwnProfileSettings {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        user.name
        user.full_name
        user.description
        user.website
        user.location
        user.pronouns
        user.visibility
        user.keep_email_private
        user.keep_pronouns_private
        user.keep_activity_private
        user.avatar_source
        user.avatar_email
        user.theme
        user.language
        user.diff_view_style
        user.enable_repo_unit_hints
        user.is_local
        config.allowed_user_visibility_modes
        config.username_cooldown_period
        config.themes

    provides:
        UserRenamesSelf(user, new_name)
            when user.is_local or user.login_source.allows_username_change
        UserUpdatesProfile(user, full_name, description, website, location, pronouns, keep_email_private, keep_pronouns_private, keep_activity_private)
        UserChangesVisibility(user, visibility)
        UserChangesTheme(user, theme)
        UserChangesLanguage(user, language)
        UserTogglesRepoUnitHints(user, enabled)
        UserChangesDiffViewStyle(user, style)
        UserHidesTimelineEvents(user, groups)
        UserChangesDiffWhitespace(user, behaviour)
        UserTogglesOutdatedComments(user, show)
        UserUploadsAvatar(user, image)
        UserChoosesEmailAvatar(user, avatar_email)
            when not config.disable_gravatar
        UserSwitchesToGeneratedAvatar(user)
        UserDeletesAvatar(user)

    @guarantee RenameWarnsAboutCooldown
        -- When a cooldown is configured, the rename form says how long the
        -- old name stays reserved for the user before others may claim it.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/settings, POST /user/settings/avatar,
        -- POST /user/settings/avatar/delete, GET /user/settings/appearance,
        -- POST /user/settings/appearance/{theme,language,hints,hidden_comments}.
        -- API: GET/PATCH /user/settings, POST/DELETE /user/avatar,
        -- GET /user (the caller's own full record).
}

-- The account holder's addresses, notification mail preference and the
-- delete-account form.
surface OwnAccountSettings {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        user.primary_email
        user.email_notifications
        for e in user.email_addresses:
            e.address
            e.is_activated
            e.is_primary
            e.can_be_primary
        user.has_feature_disabled(deletion)
        config.user_delete_with_comments_max_time

    provides:
        UserAddsEmail(user, address)
            when not config.require_email_confirmation or not activation_mail_recently_sent(user)
        UserResendsEmailActivation(user, address)
        UserMakesEmailPrimary(user, address)
        UserDeletesEmail(user, address)
        UserChangesEmailNotifications(user, preference)
        UserDeletesOwnAccount(user)
            when not deletion_disabled_for(user) and not user.is_admin

    @guarantee DeletionWarnsAboutContributions
        -- When USER_DELETE_WITH_COMMENTS_MAX_TIME is set and the account is
        -- younger than it, the form warns that comments will be deleted too.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/settings/account, POST /user/settings/account/email
        -- (_method = PRIMARY | SENDACTIVATION | NOTIFICATION | add),
        -- POST /user/settings/account/email/delete, POST /user/settings/account/delete.
        -- API: GET/POST/DELETE /user/emails.
        -- Password change on the same page belongs to authentication.
}

-- A signed-in user looking at someone's profile.
surface UserProfile {
    facing viewer: access/SignedInUser
    context profile: User where visible_to(viewer)

    exposes:
        profile.name
        profile.full_name
        profile.display_name
        profile.description
        profile.website
        profile.location
        profile.pronouns
        profile.visibility
        profile.created_at
        profile.kind
        profile.num_followers
        profile.num_following
        profile.public_email
            when config.show_user_email and not profile.keep_email_private
        for f in profile.follows_received:
            f.follower.name
                when f.follower.visible_to(viewer)
        for ub in profile.badges:
            ub.badge.description
            ub.badge.image_url

    provides:
        UserFollowsUser(viewer, profile)
            when viewer != profile
        UserUnfollowsUser(viewer, profile)
        UserBlocksUser(viewer, profile)
            when viewer != profile
        UserUnblocksUser(viewer, profile)

    @guarantee InvisibleProfilesDoNotExist
        -- A profile the viewer may not see answers exactly like a name that
        -- does not exist, including through its old names (redirects) and
        -- the .keys / .gpg / .rss / .atom / .png sub-routes.

    @guarantee ActivityRespectsPrivacy
        -- The activity tab, heatmap and feeds show nothing to others when
        -- keep_activity_private is set (admins and the user still see them).

    @guarantee ProfileReadme
        -- If the user owns a repository named ".profile" that is public, not
        -- a fork, not empty and readable by the viewer, its default branch
        -- README is rendered as the default "overview" tab, and its
        -- FUNDING file adds funding links; otherwise the repositories tab is
        -- the default.

    @guarantee OldNamesRedirect
        -- A request for an old name of a visible user redirects to the
        -- current name, keeping the rest of the path and the query.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{username} (tabs: overview, repositories, stars,
        -- watching, followers, following, activity, projects, packages,
        -- feed), GET /{username}.{keys,gpg,rss,atom,png},
        -- POST /{username} (action = follow | unfollow | block | unblock).
        -- API: GET /users/{username}, /users/{username}/followers,
        -- /users/{username}/following[/{target}], GET/PUT/DELETE
        -- /user/following/{username}, GET /user/followers,
        -- PUT /user/block/{username}, PUT /user/unblock/{username}.
        -- Location links to USER_LOCATION_MAP_URL + location.
        -- Followers / following lists only include users visible to the viewer.
        -- Organizations the user belongs to are listed: public ones to
        -- everybody, limited ones to signed-in viewers, private ones only to
        -- the user and admins.
}

-- An organization page's follow button.
surface OrganizationFollowButton {
    facing viewer: access/SignedInUser
    context organization: organizations/Organization

    provides:
        UserFollowsOrganization(viewer, organization)
        UserUnfollowsOrganization(viewer, organization)
}

-- The user's own block list.
surface OwnBlockList {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        for b in user.blocks_given:
            b.blocked.name
            b.created_at

    provides:
        UserUnblocksUser(user, blocked)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/settings/blocked_users, POST .../unblock.
        -- API: GET /user/list_blocked.
}

-- An organization's block list, managed by its owners.
surface OrganizationBlockList {
    facing owner: organizations/OrgOwner
    context organization: organizations/Organization

    provides:
        OrganizationBlocksUser(owner, organization, blocked)
        OrganizationUnblocksUser(owner, organization, blocked)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/settings/blocked_users. API: GET /orgs/{org}/list_blocked,
        -- PUT /orgs/{org}/block/{username}, PUT /orgs/{org}/unblock/{username}.
}

-- The block contract other modules must enforce. Stated here because the
-- block is defined here; each module states its own rule-level check.
surface BlockEnforcement {
    facing actor: access/SignedInUser
    context block: UserBlock where blocked = actor

    exposes:
        block.created_at

    @guarantee BlockedCannotFollow
        -- Neither side of a user-to-user block can follow the other.
    @guarantee BlockedCannotOpenIssuesOrPulls
        -- A user blocked by a repository's owner (user or organization)
        -- cannot open issues or pull requests in that repository.
    @guarantee BlockedCannotInteractWithIssue
        -- A user blocked by the repository owner or by an issue's poster
        -- cannot comment on, react to, retitle, close or reopen that issue
        -- or pull request; reacting to a comment is also refused when the
        -- comment's poster blocked them.
    @guarantee BlockedCannotCollaborate
        -- A user cannot be added as a collaborator to a repository whose
        -- owner blocked them, or whose owner they blocked.
    @guarantee BlockedCannotTransferTo
        -- A repository cannot be transferred to an owner who blocked the doer.
    @guarantee BlockIsSilent
        -- The blocked user is not told they were blocked; the refused
        -- action simply reports that the user blocked them.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred User.avatar_url              -- see: notifications / UI; resolution order in AvatarSource
deferred is_usable_username           -- see: header comment "Names"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Follow visibility: Forgejo lets anyone follow a user they cannot see (no visibility check on follow). The spec requires visibility to avoid leaking private accounts; confirm."
open question "Reserved user/organization placeholder kinds (UserTypeUserReserved/OrganizationReserved) exist in the schema with no creation path; should the rebuild offer admin-reserved names (anti re-registration) as a feature?"
open question "Admins are not immune to being blocked (TODO in services/user/block.go). Should a block prevent a site admin's actions?"
open question "Blocking does not remove the blocked user from repositories the blocker owns through an organization, nor org membership; should it?"
open question "Self-deletion is refused for site admins entirely (not only the last admin). Keep, or allow when other admins remain?"
open question "Making an address primary via the web does not re-check activation server-side (only the UI hides the button). The spec requires activation; confirm."
open question "Badges have a schema and display but no management UI or API; should the rebuild offer admin badge management?"
open question "Inactive-account cleanup runs only on its cron schedule (default yearly, disabled). Should eligibility be continuous instead?"
open question "Purge disables the account outside the deletion transaction so a failure can leave a disabled, half-purged account; should purge be resumable?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.allows_username_change: OAuth2 sources may allow users to rename themselves (UserRenamesSelf).
-- REQUEST authentication: emit RemoteUserClaimed(user, email) when an OAuth2 login matches an F3 placeholder.
-- REQUEST authentication: the password re-entry for UserDeletesOwnAccount and the "manage_password" feature flag (UserFeature) are yours.
-- REQUEST organizations: provide is_org_owner(organization, user) and shares_organization(a, b) (both users are members of a common organization, or one is the organization); react to UserPurged by removing memberships and deleting organizations where the user is the last owner; org renames should go through RenameNamespace semantics (UserRedirect with organization set); names are unique across users and organizations.
-- REQUEST organizations/Organization.follows: Follow.followee_organization relationship for follower counts on org pages.
-- REQUEST repositories: provide owns_repositories(user) (any repository with owner_user = user); used by deletion preconditions.
-- REQUEST organizations: provide belongs_to_organizations(user) (any OrgMembership of the user); used by deletion preconditions.
-- REQUEST repositories: react to UserRenamed (owner names and storage), UserBlocked / OrganizationBlockedUser (unwatch blocker-owned repos, drop collaboration, cancel pending transfers, refuse collaborator add and transfer to a blocker), UserPurged (delete owned repos), UserAccountDeleted (stars, watches, collaborations).
-- REQUEST issues: enforce BlockEnforcement on issue creation (repo owner blocked poster), comment, reaction (also comment poster), title change, status change (repo owner or issue poster blocked doer); react to UserAccountDeleted(delete_contributions, purge).
-- REQUEST pulls: refuse PR creation when the base repository owner blocked the poster; react to UserAccountDeleted (auto-merges, review state).
-- REQUEST packages: provide owns_packages(user); react to UserPurged (delete all owned packages) and UserRenamed (container image names).
-- REQUEST actions: react to UserBlocked (revoke trust of the blocked user on the blocker's repositories) and UserAccountDeleted (runners, tokens, trust).
-- REQUEST keys: react to UserAccountDeleted (SSH, GPG keys and imports; rewrite authorized keys / principals).
-- REQUEST administration: admin user management entry points stay yours; this module reacts to UserRenamedByAdmin (redirect), UserDeletedByAdmin (purge disable + cascade), UserAvatarChangedByAdmin / UserAvatarRemovedByAdmin, InactiveAccountCleanupDue(older_than).
-- REQUEST administration: AdminSetsUserPrimaryEmail must keep EmailAddress rows consistent (promote an existing address of the same user or create one, mark it primary and activated, keep the old primary as a secondary address, skip email-domain lists) and emit accounts' PrimaryEmailChanged; AdminCreatesUser must create the primary EmailAddress (activated), delete any UserRedirect for the name, and apply the same creation defaults as CreateAccountBySelfRegistration minus prefix/cooldown/domain checks.
-- REQUEST administration: AdminSetsUserAdmin / AdminDeletesUser must refuse removing the last admin (invariant AtLeastOneAdmin).
-- REQUEST notifications: send the confirmation mail on authentication/EmailConfirmationRequested (not on EmailActivationRequested), primary-change mail to the old address on PrimaryEmailChanged; honour User.email_notifications and User.can_receive_mail; honour activity_readable_by for feeds and heatmap.
-- REQUEST federation: emit RemoteActorDiscovered(handle, full_name, email); react to UserPurged (delete FederatedUser).
-- REQUEST access: anonymous visitors see only public profiles; restricted users see only public profiles (plus their own and admins' rules); expose an anonymous actor this module's profile surface can face.
-- REQUEST moderation: keep a shadow copy of a reported user's profile fields before UserProfileUpdated / PrimaryEmailChanged / deletion.
